NAME
    man - read a man page

SYNOPSIS
    man TOPIC
    man -k WORD
    man

DESCRIPTION
    Reads /man/TOPIC and writes it to stdout. With no arguments,
    lists every available topic (the contents of /man/). With
    -k WORD, lists every topic whose name contains WORD as a
    substring.

    AdventOS does NOT use Unix section numbers (man 1 cp). All
    pages live in a flat /man/ directory. Section suffixes will
    be added if a name collision ever happens.

    There is no pager — `man` is closer to `cat /man/TOPIC` than
    to GNU man's `less`-wrapped behavior. Pages are kept short
    (typically 30-60 lines) so this is usually fine. Pipe to
    `head` or `tail` if a page is longer than your screen:

        man find | head -25

EXAMPLES
    man cp
    man -k file                 # everything mentioning "file" in name
    man                         # list all topics

EXIT STATUS
    0   page found and printed (or list emitted)
    1   topic not found
    2   usage error or I/O error

SEE ALSO
    ls(1), cat(1), grep(1)

NOTES
    Page format is plain text, no markup. Standard sections:
    NAME, SYNOPSIS, DESCRIPTION, EXAMPLES, EXIT STATUS, SEE ALSO,
    NOTES. New pages should follow the same skeleton.

    To add a man page: drop the file at fs/man/<topic> and add
    it to mkfs.py's DATA_FILES list with parent='man'.
